                <p style="color: #6b7280; margin-bottom: 1rem;">By default, ConScan runs all scans. Use the <code>--scanners</code> flag to run specific checks:</p>
                <div class="code-block">
<span class="comment"># Scan only for vulnerabilities and secrets</span>
<span class="prompt">$</span> conscan scan --scanners=vuln,secret yourimage:tag

<span class="comment"># Available scanners: vuln, secret, package, cis, storage</span>
                </div>
                <h3 style="margin: 2rem 0 1rem;">Output Formats</h3>
                <div class="output-formats">
                    <div class="format-card">
                        <h4>Table (Default)</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Human-readable</li>
                            <li>CLI-friendly</li>
                            <li>Quick overview</li>
                        </ul>
                        <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
<span class="prompt">$</span> conscan scan yourimage:tag
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="format-card">
                        <h4>HTML Report</h4>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Shareable reports</li>
                            <li>Visual presentation</li>
                            <li>Team collaboration</li>
                        </ul>
                        <div class="code-block" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
<span class="prompt">$</span> conscan scan --format html --output report.html yourimage:tag
